ref 17592186045417] [17592186559765 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559287 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559765 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559765 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559765 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559765 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559765 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186559163 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559765 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f65721db-6112-5108-9ea1-45e3d318fab2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559775 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559775 #edb/ref 1069 "q-174417" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559775 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559775 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are mathematical statements?\n\n- $P:5\\,|\\,9$\n\n- $Q:\\sqrt{2}+0.2$\n\n- $R:\\sqrt{2}\\in R$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559775 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0a9725fe-5d32-5217-81b5-21b1fce3c258" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559775 #edb/ref 1074 "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options: \n\n- $P$ is a statement. This statement is *false* because $5$ does not divide $9.$\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false.\n\n- $R$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because $\\sqrt{2}$ is a real number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $R$ only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559776 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559776 #edb/ref 1069 "q-174379" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559776 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559776 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are mathematical statements?\n\n- $P:$ $0.5$ is a rational number.\n\n- $Q:$ $0.5$ is an irrational number.\n\n- $R:$ Divide $5$ by $10.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559776 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0ac2c565-7f72-5deb-8186-0f592c4c5383" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559776 #edb/ref 1074 "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options:\n\n- $P$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because $0.5=\\frac{5}{10},$ so it is a rational number.\n\n- $Q$ is a statement. This statement is *false* because $0.5$ is a rational number.\n\n- $R$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false. Rather, it is an instruction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $Q$ only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559779 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559779 #edb/ref 1069 "q-174324" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559779 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559779 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $P:$ A square has exactly four sides.\n\n- $Q:$ $7+2\\ge 10$\n\n- $R:$ $9$ is a prime number." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559779 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0f8c15c2-cbc4-5d0f-bd4c-5f44e2f7b150" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559779 #edb/ref 1074 "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate the truth value of each statement:\n\n- Statement $P$ is *true.* Indeed, A square has exactly four sides.\n\n- Statement $Q$ is *false* because $7+2=9≱10.$\n\n- Statement $R$ is *false* because $9$ is not a prime number (it is a composite number).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559799 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559799 #edb/ref 1069 "q-175327" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559799 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559799 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are mathematical predicates of one variable?\n\nI. $z$ divided by $10.$\n\nII. $x\\times 3$\n\nIII. $y+3$ is an odd number." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559799 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3bd80b9b-2655-5bf4-bdf9-f7428c6e7e13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559799 #edb/ref 1074 "A *predicate* of one variable is a sentence that contains the variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute any concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $z$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $y$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559805 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559730 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559805 #edb/ref 1069 "q-174421" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559805 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559805 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are mathematical statements?\n\n- $P:\\{2,3,7\\}\\cap \\{3,5,6\\}=∅$\n\n- $Q:{\\pi }^{2}-\\pi $\n\n- $R:3$ is a prime number." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559805 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4681538e-2de2-56f3-881c-562aebb342a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559805 #edb/ref 1074 "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options: \n\n- $P$ is a statement. This statement is *false* because the intersection of the given sets is the set $\\{3\\}.$\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false.\n\n- $R$ is a statement. This statement is *true* since $3$ is indeed a prime number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $R$ only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559841 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559841 #edb/ref 1069 "q-174322" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559841 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559841 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $P:$ $2>6$\n\n- $Q:$ $10$ is an integer number.\n\n- $R:$ $7$ is a composite number." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559841 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ae278ad9-7ac4-5180-982a-a8a5385a7ed1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559841 #edb/ref 1074 "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate the truth value of each statement:\n\n- Statement $P$ is *false* because $2≯6.$\n\n- Statement $Q$ is *true.* Indeed, $10$ is an integer number.\n\n- Statement $R$ is *false* because $7$ is not a composite number (it is a prime number).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Q$ only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559843 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559736 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559843 #edb/ref 1069 "q-102847" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559843 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559843 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is a mathematical statement?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559843 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ae9ba4f6-2cb2-5711-bd11-5c1b1d70436a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559843 #edb/ref 1074 "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false. \n\nOf the given sentences, the only sentence that is either true or false is \"A rectangle has four angles.\" (This sentence is true.)\n\nAll the other sentences are neither true nor false." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559852 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559852 #edb/ref 1069 "q-86474" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559852 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559852 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is a mathematical statement?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559852 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c043e0c4-50de-5146-885c-1db3a041b406" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559852 #edb/ref 1074 "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false. \n\nOf the given sentences, the only sentence that is either true or false is \"$3$ is a positive number.\" (This sentence is true.)\n\nAll the other sentences are neither true nor false." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559865 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559865 #edb/ref 1069 "q-173721" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559865 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559865 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are false?\n\n- $P:$ $\\sqrt{5}$ is a real number.\n\n- $Q:$ $10$ is divisible by $3.$\n\n- $R:$ $2+3\\le 1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559865 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d4bf832a-fa7c-5bf9-96bc-b8972c38ecca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559865 #edb/ref 1074 "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate the truth value of each statement:\n\n- Statement $P$ is *true.* Indeed, $\\sqrt{5}$ is a real number.\n\n- Statement $Q$ is *false* because $10$ is not divisible by $3.$\n\n- Statement $R$ is *false* because $2+3=5≰1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Q$ and $R$ only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559866 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559866 #edb/ref 1069 "q-102854" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559866 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559866 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the truth value of the following mathematical statement?\n\n$\\,$ Half of $10$ is $5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559866 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d625ae65-2877-56d1-acca-93794ab5d50e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559866 #edb/ref 1074 "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nThis statement is true because the $10÷2=5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559869 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559869 #edb/ref 1069 "q-174325" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559869 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559869 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are false?\n\n- $P:$ $\\sqrt{2}=1$\n\n- $Q:$ ${3}^{2}=9$\n\n- $R:$ $8$ is a composite number." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559869 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dd39dbfa-f77c-5216-9581-0acf72d83216" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559869 #edb/ref 1074 "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate the truth value of each statement:\n\n- Statement $P$ is *false* because $\\sqrt{2}\\ne 1.$\n\n- Statement $Q$ is *true.* Indeed, ${3}^{2}=9.$\n\n- Statement $R$ is *true.* Indeed, $8$ is a composite number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559884 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559755 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559884 #edb/ref 1069 "q-175340" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559884 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559884 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are mathematical predicates of one variable?\n\nI. $P(n):$ ${n}^{2}$ is odd.\n\nII. $Q(x):$ $(x+2)|5$\n\nIII. $R(y):$ $y$ is a multiple of $4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559884 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f4fa3c45-5e91-57f0-a165-1adda22fdfd5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559884 #edb/ref 1074 "A *predicate* of one variable is a sentence that contains the variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute any concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $n$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $y$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
